# Copy to ~/.lobster-tools.conf and edit. Every setting can also be given as a flag on the command
# line, which wins over this file, or as an environment variable (LOBSTER_<SETTING>), which wins
# over this file too. This file is read, never run: KEY=value lines, # comments, optional quotes,
# and a leading ~ in a path means your home folder. Only what belongs to this machine goes here;
# nothing secret.
#
# The folder that holds every project's mailbox (lobster-mail). It must be reachable from every
# machine or shell that sends or reads mail; in Claude's Linux device shell that is the mounted
# path, e.g. ~/mnt/mail.
#MAIL_ROOT=~/projects/mail
